# --- Licensed source data: present locally, never committed ---
# The full LOINC release, downloaded by whoever holds the licence for this deployment.
# LOINC is free to use with attribution, but redistribution of the complete table is
# restricted, and this repository is public. Only the subset AMRIT binds to ships, inside
# shared/terminology/terminology-seed.v1.json, which is what DATA_LICENCES.md describes.
# tools/generate_terminology_seed.py reads this directory when it is present.
Loinc/
Loinc_*.zip

# --- FHIR IG build output ---
# The IG Publisher writes ~310 MB per build into these three directories, and none of it is
# source: `fsh-generated/` and `input/` are, and they stay tracked.
#
# `input-cache/txcache` is the reason this section is not merely about repository size. It is
# 35 MB of cached responses from tx.fhir.org — whole CodeSystem fragments, including LOINC and
# SNOMED content pulled in during validation. The same restriction that keeps the full LOINC
# release out of this repository applies to a cache of it arriving by a different route, and
# this repository is public. The IG's own published artefacts are the bound subsets and are
# fine: the expansions ship 914 LOINC susceptibility concepts and 3 observation concepts,
# which is what the exporter binds and what DATA_LICENCES.md describes.
fhir-ig/output/
fhir-ig/temp/
fhir-ig/input-cache/
# The publisher expands `fhir.base.template#current` (see ig.ini) into here. It is a fetched
# template cache like the three above, not anything authored in this repository.
fhir-ig/template/

# --- Study outputs ---
# The benchmark writes shard reports and merged results here. They are regenerated by
# `paper/analysis/run_study_e.sh` from seeds held in the repository, and the versions that
# back the manuscripts are deposited with the papers rather than carried in the tree.
paper/results/

# --- Tooling output ---
graphify-out/
.graphify_python
.claude/
~$*.docx

# --- Stale build artifact (duplicate of Server/) ---
Server.zip
